WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.153
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:16.726
Unit sixteen: Consumer Behavior. Today you will analyse motivations with what + influences / drives + noun.

4
00:00:17.026 --> 00:00:19.643
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.798
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.081
Consumer behavior.

7
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:31.196
Consumer behavior means the study of how people choose, buy and use products.

8
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:35.025
Consumer behavior changed rapidly during the pandemic.

9
00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:38.432
Your turn. Say: Consumer behavior.

10
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.871
Consumer behavior.

11
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:44.931
Purchase decision.

12
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:49.066
Purchase decision means the final choice to buy a product.

13
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.230
Reviews strongly affect the purchase decision.

14
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.980
Your turn. Say: Purchase decision.

15
00:00:58.833 --> 00:01:00.032
Purchase decision.

16
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.098
Brand perception.

17
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:05.977
Brand perception means how consumers view a brand.

18
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:09.825
Brand perception improved after the charity campaign.

19
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:13.197
Your turn. Say: Brand perception.

20
00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.406
Brand perception.

21
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.314
Motivation.

22
00:01:20.317 --> 00:01:23.373
Motivation means the reason behind a person's action.

23
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.225
Status is a powerful motivation for buying luxury goods.

24
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:30.434
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

25
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.417
Motivation.

26
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.184
Buying journey.

27
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:40.878
Buying journey means the stages a customer goes through before buying.

28
00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:43.982
For cars, the buying journey can last months.

29
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:47.329
Your turn. Say: Buying journey.

30
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:51.435
Buying journey.

31
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.510
Loyalty program.

32
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:58.014
Loyalty program means a scheme that rewards repeat customers.

33
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:01.928
The café's loyalty program offers every tenth drink free.

34
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:05.761
Your turn. Say: Loyalty program.

35
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.193
Loyalty program.

36
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.706
Psychology of pricing.

37
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:18.201
Psychology of pricing means how price presentation affects buyers' perception.

38
00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:23.370
The psychology of pricing explains why $9.99 feels cheaper.

39
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:27.216
Your turn. Say: Psychology of pricing.

40
00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.869
Psychology of pricing.

41
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:33.769
Influence.

42
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:38.072
Influence means the power to affect someone's choices.

43
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:41.054
Friends have more influence than adverts.

44
00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.931
Your turn. Say: Influence.

45
00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:47.907
Influence.

46
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.490
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:59.195
Visal, your survey asked students in Phnom Penh how they choose a smartphone. What did you discover?

48
00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:08.207
What drives the purchase decision varies by person. For some it's the camera; for others it's what their friends own.

49
00:03:09.317 --> 00:03:10.887
Did price matter most?

50
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:23.703
Less than expected. What really influences young buyers is social proof: reviews, TikTok videos and recommendations from peers.

51
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:27.339
So advertising is becoming less important?

52
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:35.177
Traditional advertising is. What persuades people now is authentic content from someone they trust.

53
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:37.973
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:42.976
Grammar focus: What plus influences and drives plus noun.

55
00:03:43.276 --> 00:03:44.532
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:45.217 --> 00:03:48.180
What drives a purchase decision varies by person.

57
00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:52.116
What really influences young buyers is social proof.

58
00:03:53.017 --> 00:03:55.806
What persuades people now is authentic content.

59
00:03:56.767 --> 00:04:06.095
A 'what' clause acts as a singular subject, so use a singular verb: What drives buyers IS price (not 'are'). It is a useful way to emphasise the key factor.

60
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.524
Be careful! Don't say: What drive buyers is price.

61
00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.896
Say: What drives buyers is price.

62
00:04:15.196 --> 00:04:17.137
'What' clause takes singular verb.

63
00:04:17.933 --> 00:04:21.201
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.593
Why We Really Buy.

65
00:04:23.893 --> 00:04:29.132
Consumer behaviour research shows that purchase decisions are far less rational than people believe.

66
00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:36.371
What influences a buyer is often emotion, habit or social pressure rather than a careful comparison of features.

67
00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:45.636
The psychology of pricing demonstrates this clearly: a price of $9.99 is perceived as significantly lower than $10.

68
00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:53.033
Loyalty programs exploit our desire for rewards, while reviews reduce the uncertainty that makes us hesitate.

69
00:04:54.033 --> 00:05:00.967
Understanding what genuinely motivates customers allows companies to design products, and messages, that fit real human behaviour.

70
00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:05.906
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.504
What drives most buyers blank convenience.

72
00:05:09.804 --> 00:05:12.529
A, are. B, is. C, be.

73
00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.753
The answer is B: is.

74
00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:22.158
The stages a customer goes through before buying form the blank.

75
00:05:22.458 --> 00:05:27.482
A, buying journey. B, loyalty program. C, motivation.

76
00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.114
The answer is A: buying journey.

77
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.352
How price presentation affects perception is the blank.

78
00:05:37.652 --> 00:05:43.036
A, brand perception. B, influence. C, psychology of pricing.

79
00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.215
The answer is C: psychology of pricing.

80
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.233
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:52.533 --> 00:05:59.577
A, What persuade me is reviews.. B, What persuades me is reviews.. C, What does persuade me are reviews is..

82
00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:06.503
The answer is B: What persuades me is reviews..

83
00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:11.983
According to the reading, $9.99 is perceived as…

84
00:06:12.283 --> 00:06:19.338
A, exactly the same as $10. B, significantly lower than $10. C, more expensive.

85
00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.513
The answer is B: significantly lower than $10.

86
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.049
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:31.883 --> 00:06:34.951
What influences your own purchase decisions the most?

88
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.320
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:53.620 --> 00:07:33.362
What influences my purchase decisions most is the experience of people I trust. Before buying anything expensive, such as headphones or a laptop, I read reviews and ask friends who already own the product. Advertising rarely persuades me, because I know it presents only the positive side. However, I admit that price psychology affects me too; discounts ending in .99 sometimes make me buy things I don't need. Recognising these influences helps me spend more carefully and avoid impulse purchases.

90
00:07:33.662 --> 00:07:35.534
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:41.680
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and what plus influences and drives plus noun.

92
00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:46.165
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

93
00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:49.140
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.197
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

